Given an array of integers in the following JSON format:
{
  "array": [5, 2, 9, 1, 5, 6]
}
How can I write a C++ program that implements the bubble sort algorithm to sort the integers in ascending order, while minimizing memory usage and avoiding potential errors?
Also, can you provide an example of how this program could be integrated into a larger program, such as a job application system, and how it could handle JSON data input and output?

response:
Here's a C++ program implementing the bubble sort algorithm for your given JSON data:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <string>
#include <fstream>
#include <nlohmann/json.hpp>
using json = nlohmann::json;

void bubbleSort(std::vector<int>& arr) {
    int n = arr.size();
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
                std::swap(arr[j], arr[j + 1]);
            }
        }
    }
}

int main() {
    std::ifstream file("input.json");
    std::string jsonString;
    file.seekg(0, std::ios::end);
    jsonString.reserve(file.tellg());
    file.seekg(0, std::ios::beg);
    file.read(&jsonString[0], file.tellg());
    file.close();

    json jsonObj = json::parse(jsonString);
    std::vector<int> arr = jsonObj["array"].get<std::vector<int>>();

    bubbleSort(arr);

    std::ofstream outputFile("output.json");
    json outputJson = {{"array", arr}};
    outputFile << outputJson.dump(4);
    outputFile.close();

    return 0;
}
```

This program reads the JSON input from a file, extracts the integer array, sorts it using the bubble sort algorithm, and writes the sorted array back to a new JSON file. To integrate this program into a larger job application system, you can modify the input and output file names according to your needs. This program can handle JSON data input and output efficiently and with minimal memory usage.

