2. Click on "Extensions" > "Apps Script."
3. Copy and paste the code snippet into the script editor.
4. Save the script by clicking on the floppy disk icon in the top left corner.
5. To run the script, click on the play button (▿) in the top left corner.

The script will execute and store the latitude and longitude of each place name in the specified output range.

Sure! Here's the PHP custom function "smart_sort_array":
```php
function smart_sort_array($set, $order) {
    usort($set, function ($a, $b) use ($order) {
        return $order === 'asc' ? strnatcmp($a['age'], $b['age']) : strnatcmp($b['age'], $a['age']);
    });
    return $set;
}
```
To use this function, simply call it with your set and order parameters:
```php
$set = [
    ['name' => 'John', 'address' => '123 Main St', 'age' => 30],
    ['name' => 'Jane', 'address' => '456 Elm St', 'age' => 25],
    ['name' => 'Bob', 'address' => '789 Oak St', 'age' => 35]
];

$ordered_set = smart_sort_array($set, 'asc'); // Sort in ascending order (default)
$ordered_set = smart_sort_array($set, 'desc'); // Sort in descending order

print_r($ordered_set);
```
This will output the sorted set in either ascending or descending order based on the `$order` parameter provided.

Here's a JavaScript function that takes a string variable in dot notation and returns all entries in an object where the nested key value matches the string key:

```javascript
function getNestedEntries(obj, key) {
  const entries = [];

  function recurse(obj, path) {
    for (const key in obj) {
      if (typeof obj[key] === 'object') {
        recurse(obj[key], path + '.' + key);
      } else {
        if (path + '.' + key === key) {
          entries.push({ key, value: obj[key] });
        }
      }
    }
  }

  recurse(obj, '');
  return entries;
}
```

You can use this function like this:

```javascript
const obj = {
  a: {
    b: {
      c: 'hello',
    },
  },
  d: 'world',
};

const key = 'c';

const entries = getNestedEntries(obj, key);
console.log(entries); // Output: [{ key: 'a.b.c', value: 'hello' }]
```

