To pass credentials in JavaScript code using `react-native-fbsdk-next`, you can follow these steps:

1. First, make sure you have installed the required dependencies by running the following command:

```bash
npm install react-native-fbsdk-next
```

2. Next, create a new file named `Credentials.js` and add the following code:

```javascript
import { Facebook } from 'react-native-fbsdk';

const Credentials = {
  appId: 'YOUR_APP_ID',
  apiKey: 'YOUR_API_KEY',
};

export default Credentials;
```

Replace `YOUR_APP_ID` and `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual Facebook app ID and API key.

3. Now, import the `Credentials` object in your main component and use it when initializing the Facebook SDK:

```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { Facebook } from 'react-native-fbsdk';
import Credentials from './Credentials';

const App = () => {
  const [isLoggedIn, setIsLoggedIn] = useState(false);

  const handleLogin = async () => {
    try {
      await Facebook.loginWithReadPermissionsAsync(Credentials.appId);
      setIsLoggedIn(true);
    } catch (error) {
      console.log('Error logging in: ', error);
    }
  };

  return (
    <View>
      {!isLoggedIn && (
        <Button title="Log in with Facebook" onPress={handleLogin} />
      )}
      {isLoggedIn && (
        <Text>Logged in successfully!</Text>
      )}
    </View>
  );
};

export default App;
```

Now, you have passed your Facebook app ID and API key in the JavaScript code using `react-native-fbsdk-next`. This will allow you to authenticate users with their Facebook accounts in your React Native app.

